  "project-delivery-disposition" [label="Delivery and\narchive\nBLOCKED", shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#fce9e5", color="#ba6251", tooltip="Establish current administrative status and requirements first; do not infer an outstanding hand-in from old deadline/unsubmitted notes. Prepare the accepted continuation/archive payload with rights/data dispositions, exact reviewed commit, checked PDF, inventory/hashes and metadata. External submission/publication remains a separate Jörn-authorized action.\nblocker: Current submission status/rules and closure-time payload/rights/data review are unverified; no release candidate or external action is selected.\nplan_gap: Accepted Zenodo direction is not a created/published record or DOI. Current closure can record an already-completed administrative action once verified.\nproject: release\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped. The oct04-candidate restart authorizes bounded thesis/repository improvement until 02:00 UTC; human PASS, public release and university submission are not implied.\nSources: docs/project-facts.md, submit/archive-closure-checklist.md, docs/reproducibility.md", penwidth=2, fontsize=14];
  "project-close" [label="Project close\nBLOCKED", shape=box, fillcolor="#fce9e5", color="#ba6251", tooltip="Coordinator reconciles selected outcomes and caveats, current scientific synthesis when its sources/route change, retained completion evidence and continuation constraints; release all project-owned assignments/sessions. Optional research remains explicitly disposed rather than silently included.\nblocker: Restart candidate integrated and its assignments released; broader workflow activation, human PASS, full reproduction and actual delivery/archive dispositions remain unfinished.\nproject: msc-math\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped. The oct04-candidate restart authorizes bounded thesis/repository improvement until 02:00 UTC; human PASS, public release and university submission are not implied.\nSources: docs/coordination/README.md, docs/coordination/handoff.md, docs/project-facts.md"];
  "coordination-load-watch" [label="Load supervision\nPARKED", shape=box, fillcolor="#f1f0ed", color="#93918c", tooltip="Read-only checker integrated and independently reviewed; 13 focused tests pass. Bounded observer interrupted after Jörn ended the discussion; full planned watch not established. Last retained 17:30:52Z snapshot had no errors/advisory signals; overload and semantic queue unknown. Observer role lacked native send tools; TUI report transport worked. Early second observation revealed interrupted-sleep cadence error, corrected to absolute targets.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Selected bounded implementation and supervision; four observations over about twelve minutes, no permanent service or thesis execution.\nnext_step: Start another bounded watch only during selected ongoing work; retain current unknowns and use verified available return transport.\nSources: scripts/coordination-load.py, scripts/test_coordination_load.py, docs/coordination/README.md"];
  "__completed" [label="DONE · owners released\nShared coordination\nLocal guidance\nWorkstation OTel\nSkill proposal\nKnowledge proposal\nProposal integration\nSemantic project map\nSupport-route proposal\nAccounting proposal\nProject completion map\nCode and evidence\nSource repairs\nClaims supported\nFrozen candidate\nFoundations and finite-capacity proof exposition\nRepository navigation and evidence ownership\nIndependent cross-chapter claim review\nDeliver revised thesis PDF and repository before 04:00 Berlin\nIndependent product-theorem review\nPreserve interrupted work and prepare an honest restart handoff\nAssemble and integrate one checked candidate\nIndependently review science, code contract and exact PDF\nObserve actual integration queue and orchestration outcomes\nRepair evidence routing and reproduction documentation\nRepair and inspect selected PDF layout\nCorrect wider action-window enumeration contract\nIndependently inspect changed mathematical interfaces", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#e7f1e8", color="#93918c", tooltip="Separate coordination, browser views and reusable knowledge\nCanonical coordination and browser source contract complete; five HTTP checks passed. Prior Chrome inspection unavailable.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/README.md, docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/coordination/handoff.md\n\nRoute process knowledge into project collaboration guidance\nLocal collaboration rules and knowledge routing complete; link/state checks passed. Behavioral and post-compaction performance untested.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: AGENTS.md, AGENTS.md.commentary.md, docs/knowledge/README.md\n\nSet up authorized workstation-only OpenObserve telemetry\nLive workstation logs/traces/metrics API-verified after daemon restart. Host implementation complete; maintenance belongs to ~/.dotfiles/INSTALL.md. Browser login unverified.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/development-environments.md, docs/coordination/otel-design.md\n\nPrepare repository-owned skill migration\nReviewable local skill/discovery migration proposal returned; planner assignment ended. Candidate, activation and fresh-client acceptance remain unselected.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/skill-migration-plan.md\n\nPlan process-knowledge cleanup and behavioural evaluation\nReviewable two-link cleanup and bounded forward-pilot proposal returned; planner assignment ended. Cleanup and pilot remain unselected.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/knowledge-evaluation-plan.md\n\nReview and consolidate returned skill and knowledge proposals\nReviewed migration and knowledge proposals against returned environment/accounting findings. Recommend nine project-local skills with Claude adapters, conditional host capabilities and retained-packet handoffs; defer controlled behavioral pilot and new messaging infrastructure. Concrete package selection remains Jörn’s decision; no skill activation or execution approval is inferred.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/skill-migration-plan.md, docs/coordination/knowledge-evaluation-plan.md\n\nSemantic msc-math project map dashboard\nSemantic DOM portfolio view completed in dedicated design session: whole msc-math goal, completion branches, interactive outcome/status/owner/blocker/scope/evidence/next-step nodes and shared prerequisite links. Live desktop/390px and320px fixture checked; no horizontal overflow.15second refresh preserves open state/focus. Root integrated source/dependency checks and8 HTTP tests.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/README.md\n\nDefine support and handoff routes across selected environments\nRead-only supported-route matrix returned: local .agents source plus proposed Claude links/import; retained packets and manual host handoff initially. Independent-thread live delivery and SSH persistence remain unverified; Codex Cloud privileged-image/R2 bootstrap assumptions are not validated for Claude.\nplan_gap: Claude fresh-clone setup/discovery, cloud-to-host handoff, remote-device review access and reconnect/session continuity have no agreed acceptance route. Required support versus explicitly deferred capabilities is unresolved.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/development-environments.md, docs/coordination/skill-migration-plan.md\n\nDefine truthful usage and spending observations\nRead-only recommendation returned: current.json and retained outcomes own durable PM state; OpenObserve is diagnostic. Optional explicit packet-event JSONL-to-OTel helper only if selected; no broker/database. Token/time observations are not billing; quota/USD unknown and independent-root/cloud usage is not covered.\nplan_gap: Comparable cloud/Pro usage, semantic task/message journaling and budget-enforcement mechanics are undefined. Numeric thresholds are not agreed; the selected delivery may explicitly defer automation.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: AGENTS.md.commentary.md, docs/development-environments.md\n\nWhole-project completion map and dependency projection\nWhole msc-math outcome/dependency map retained: workflow subproject, thesis support/prose and human PASS, code/evidence, reproduction, actual delivery/archive and closure. Twelve independent read-only candidates plus optional research/writing routes are visible without execution authorization. Semantic dashboard is primary; DOT/SVG source-hash projection checks pass.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/README.md\n\nRetained implementation and artifact claims match their support\nCurrent candidate code/artifact claims received bounded source, count, path and API-contract review; two numerical defects repaired, all 52 literal local path occurrences resolve, retained exact evidence verified. Flow production correspondence remains explicitly bounded; this is not a whole-implementation proof.\nplan_gap: No need for blanket code cleanup or a universal solver formalization; inspect exactly what retained claims require.\nproject: evidence\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped. The oct04-candidate restart authorizes bounded thesis/repository improvement until 02:00 UTC; human PASS, public release and university submission are not implied.\nSources: docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/acceptance-numerical.md, docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/acceptance-source-review.md\n\nClose surviving source repairs and reader-comment dispositions\nAll seven selected-source obligations dispositioned against the final candidate, including DS comment mapping and rendered L10-N/N+ scope/caveats. Whole-chapter human acceptance and overall DS scope remain separate unknowns.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped. The oct04-candidate restart authorizes bounded thesis/repository improvement until 02:00 UTC; human PASS, public release and university submission are not implied.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/ds-comment-disposition.md, docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/acceptance-source-review.md\n\nAudit selected theorem and empirical wording against evidence\nAll 11 required areas mapped against selected sources, final PDF and evidence. Independent bounded reviews found no remaining blocking scoped finding; fixed-facet/equality/upper-section, empirical and conditional-flow limitations preserved. No unrestricted verification or human PASS implied.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped. The oct04-candidate restart authorizes bounded thesis/repository improvement until 02:00 UTC; human PASS, public release and university submission are not implied.\nSources: docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/acceptance-source-review.md, docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/acceptance-pdf.md, docs/project-facts.md\n\nAssemble and inspect one exact reader-facing candidate\nOne retained100-page candidate, PDF 27dbf152… and source ac7f7765…, built and independently reviewed with exact manifests. Historical docs/resume remains unchanged; new candidate identity checker passes.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped. The oct04-candidate restart authorizes bounded thesis/repository improvement until 02:00 UTC; human PASS, public release and university submission are not implied.\nSources: docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/candidate-manifest.json, docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/acceptance-manifest.json, thesis/README.md\n\nFoundations and finite-capacity proof exposition\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Historical initial-run assignment stopped and preserved in fe3475b3. Current integration/acceptance is owned by the separately authorized restart tasks.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: thesis/chapters/04-quadratic-program.tex\n\nRepository navigation and evidence ownership\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Historical initial-run assignment stopped and preserved in fe3475b3. Current integration/acceptance is owned by the separately authorized restart tasks.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: formal/FINDINGS.md, docs/knowledge/README.md\n\nIndependent cross-chapter claim review\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Historical initial-run assignment stopped and preserved in fe3475b3. Current integration/acceptance is owned by the separately authorized restart tasks.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: thesis/chapters/01-introduction.tex, thesis/chapters/16-conclusion.tex\n\nDeliver revised thesis PDF and repository before 04:00 Berlin\nDelivered retained100-page candidate and repository improvements, preserving fe3475b3. Independent scoped acceptance, six repaired findings, passing numerical/build/source checks, same-environment source-only rebuild and truthful caveats retained.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Jörn explicitly restarted from fe3475b3 on 4 October 2026: best supported thesis PDF/repository using remaining weekly quota (numeric balance unknown), no human questions, absolute stop 2026-10-04T02:00:00Z. No public release or university submission.\nnext_step: No restart work remains assigned. Human PASS, broader DS scope and full fresh-environment/data reproduction remain separate unknowns.\nSources: docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/README.md, docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/candidate-manifest.json, docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/acceptance-manifest.json\n\nIndependent product-theorem review\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Original task stopped; no running assignment.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: docs/coordination/restart-2026-10-04.md\n\nPreserve interrupted work and prepare an honest restart handoff\nConcrete continuation packet, independent evidence/design/custody reviews and preservation checkpoint. Proposed orchestration untested; no thesis acceptance or restart implied.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Historical four-minute handoff completed; checkpoint preserved. Subsequent direct instruction authorized the restart.\nSources: docs/coordination/restart-2026-10-04.md\n\nAssemble and integrate one checked candidate\nIntegrated preserved checkpoint and corrections into final 100-page PDF; all 11 required areas, source backlog and96-source scientific baseline reconciled. No further consequential in-scope defect; own workers released.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Jörn explicitly restarted from fe3475b3 on 4 October 2026: best supported thesis PDF/repository using remaining weekly quota (numeric balance unknown), no human questions, absolute stop 2026-10-04T02:00:00Z. No public release or university submission.\nnext_step: Assignment closed; retained report states exact checked scope and limitations.\nSources: docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/integration.md\n\nIndependently review science, code contract and exact PDF\nFinal27dbf152… PDF independently accepted for bounded review-candidate delivery: all 100 pages read/overview-rendered,64 individually inspected, all 11 areas mapped, six findings closed. Human PASS remains unknown.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Jörn explicitly restarted from fe3475b3 on 4 October 2026: best supported thesis PDF/repository using remaining weekly quota (numeric balance unknown), no human questions, absolute stop 2026-10-04T02:00:00Z. No public release or university submission.\nnext_step: Assignment closed; retained report states exact checked scope and limitations.\nSources: docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/acceptance-manifest.json\n\nObserve actual integration queue and orchestration outcomes\nWatch ended 00:52:07 UTC. Direct integration and independent correction cycles observed; no abandoned ready packet observed. One short verifier rerun duplicated; root context grew. Sustained effectiveness/efficiency and forced-stop behavior unestablished; pending_init child metadata remains ambiguous after explicit release/interrupt.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Jörn explicitly restarted from fe3475b3 on 4 October 2026: best supported thesis PDF/repository using remaining weekly quota (numeric balance unknown), no human questions, absolute stop 2026-10-04T02:00:00Z. No public release or university submission.\nnext_step: Assignment closed; retained report states exact checked scope and limitations.\nSources: docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/supervision.md\n\nRepair evidence routing and reproduction documentation\nAccepted documentation packet: INSTALL semantic review, non-HKO nested-archive routing with hashes and fresh bounded exact/independent checks, reproduction semantics, DS and visualization navigation. Eight dashboard HTTP tests passed before later root source-status change.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Bounded child assignment within authorized restart, no human questions; absolute stop 02:00 UTC.\nnext_step: Assignment closed; retained report states exact checked scope and limitations.\nSources: docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/evidence-docs.md\n\nRepair and inspect selected PDF layout\nAccepted source packet: three artifact-path overflow repairs and small summary clarifications; isolated101-page build warning-free and selected pages inspected. Independent assembled review later found orphaned ToC entry, now handled by integration.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Bounded child assignment within authorized restart, no human questions; absolute stop 02:00 UTC.\nnext_step: Assignment closed; retained report states exact checked scope and limitations.\nSources: docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/thesis-layout.md\n\nCorrect wider action-window enumeration contract\nWider action-window pruning and singular exact-tube consistency repaired and independently reviewed. Public API 15/15, correspondence 4/4, full library 376 passed, 23 ignored. Scalar-capacity error and synthetic singular-case polytope reachability not established.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Bounded child assignment within authorized restart, no human questions; absolute stop 02:00 UTC.\nnext_step: Assignment closed; retained report states exact checked scope and limitations.\nSources: docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/acceptance-numerical.md\n\nIndependently inspect changed mathematical interfaces\nBounded source/paper/proof interface and final pages8–41 review completed, plus independent numerical-patch check. No remaining scoped blocker. Child explicitly released/interrupted; native pending_init metadata does not establish a completed process state.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Bounded child assignment within authorized restart, no human questions; absolute stop 02:00 UTC.\nnext_step: Assignment closed; retained report states exact checked scope and limitations.\nSources: docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/acceptance-source-review.md"];
  "__parked" [label="UNSELECTED / PARKED · no execution\nCommunication diagnosis · BLOCKED\nSkill migration candidate · PARKED\nKnowledge cleanup / pilot · PARKED\nCloud automation · PARKED\nHistorical stop respected · DONE\nOptional result routes · PARKED\nOpen research packages · PARKED\nWriting method trial · PARKED\nLocal-maximality proofs and certificate navigation · DONE\nExact product-family proofs · DONE\nEmpirical interpretation and numerical example · DONE\nReproduction and evidence availability · DONE\nIndependent local-theorem review · DONE\nNumerical API-contract review · DONE", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#f1f0ed", color="#93918c", tooltip="Determine why agent communication tools failed\nBounded local diagnosis finished. Same daemon persisted through failures; multiple TUI MCP server processes turned over. Stale endpoint binding is plausible, but old-port ownership, shutdown/rebind evidence and original cause are unavailable. Current list verifies reads only.\nblocker: Historical endpoint ownership/binding evidence is unavailable; current successful reads do not establish original cause or legacy send recovery.\nplan_gap: Capture failing URL, socket owner/PID and endpoint-binding lifecycle events on the next natural failure. Do not launch repeated investigation or restart the shared daemon.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/current.json\n\nOptional local skill candidate, activation and fresh-client tests\nProposed nine-skill local package, Claude discovery adapters and focused acceptance route. Keep outside loaded paths until selected. This is a candidate route, not an assignment.\nplan_gap: Initial instruction was inspect/plan/discuss first; migration and activation selection absent.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/skill-migration-plan.md\n\nOptional knowledge cleanup and forward pilot\nChoose retain-and-observe, two-link cleanup only, or cleanup plus bounded A/E pilot. No model calls or cleanup are launched by this plan.\nplan_gap: Scope, owner and resources have not been selected; broader cases and post-compaction validation remain unperformed.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/knowledge-evaluation-plan.md\n\nPossible cloud communication, setup and accounting automation\nExternal surfaces remain outside workstation telemetry. Live cloud messaging, detailed returned event logs and enforcement are possible mechanisms; required support and value are undecided.\nplan_gap: No agreed need, design, acceptance contract or authorization for cloud automation.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/development-environments.md\n\nPrevious thesis stop superseded by 4 October authorization\nThe previous stop was respected until Jörn authorized this new bounded thesis/repository run. This historical task is closed; oct04-candidate owns current execution.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Historical stop respected until explicit restart; oct04-candidate owns current scope.\nSources: docs/coordination/handoff.md\n\nReview optional research/result selection\nReviewed but unselected results include the fixed-pentagon/symmetric-partner bound, harmonic blind directions, ridge circulation, moment counterexample and joint-representation separations. Research validity/interest is not thesis selection or novelty acceptance.\nplan_gap: No exact optional result is selected for integration; the general zonotope bound remains conjectural/paused.\nproject: research\nauthorization: Unselected optional work; not a thesis-completion prerequisite or execution authorization.\nnext_step: Select a bounded statement/evidence/value comparison before any research execution or thesis addition.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md\n\nStructure a bounded future mathematical research packet\nThe dated scientific view records F=11/global HKO questions as outside the submission route; project facts distinguish non-generic arbitrary-polytope support from generic smooth-branch results. These are possible future questions, not current theorem obligations or assigned experiments.\nplan_gap: Exact question, owner evidence baseline, useful alternatives and resources have not been selected; recheck source owners before promoting historical open questions.\nproject: research\nauthorization: Unselected optional work; not a thesis-completion prerequisite or execution authorization.\nnext_step: Select a bounded problem-structuring packet; no large proof search, producer or Pro handoff follows automatically.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md, docs/dashboard/thesis.html\n\nConsider a discriminating authoring-workflow trial\nA current-source passage trial may inform authoring value, but local trials cannot certify whole-thesis readiness. Source repairs have independent value and do not depend on this optional mechanism.\nplan_gap: No trial candidate, success criterion, cost or human-review package selected; retrospective writing outcomes are not a general reliable method.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected optional work; not a thesis-completion prerequisite or execution authorization.\nnext_step: Select a concrete trial only if it could change the authoring route enough to justify its cost.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md\n\nLocal-maximality proofs and certificate navigation\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Historical initial-run assignment stopped and preserved in fe3475b3. Current integration/acceptance is owned by the separately authorized restart tasks.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: thesis/chapters/07-hko.tex\n\nExact product-family proofs\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Historical initial-run assignment stopped and preserved in fe3475b3. Current integration/acceptance is owned by the separately authorized restart tasks.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: thesis/chapters/09-rotated-regular-polygons.tex, thesis/chapters/10-affine-pentagons.tex, thesis/chapters/11-product-position.tex\n\nEmpirical interpretation and numerical example\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Historical initial-run assignment stopped and preserved in fe3475b3. Current integration/acceptance is owned by the separately authorized restart tasks.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: thesis/chapters/08-data-science.tex, thesis/chapters/13-numerics.tex\n\nReproduction and evidence availability\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Historical initial-run assignment stopped and preserved in fe3475b3. Current integration/acceptance is owned by the separately authorized restart tasks.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: thesis/chapters/14-code-data.tex, INSTALL.md\n\nIndependent local-theorem review\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Original task stopped; no running assignment.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: docs/coordination/restart-2026-10-04.md\n\nNumerical API-contract review\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Original task stopped; no running assignment.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: docs/coordination/restart-2026-10-04.md"];
  "__candidates_thesis" [label="THESIS · READY IF SELECTED\nFoundations / QP\nVariation / certificate\nProduct proof bridges\nDS reader disposition\nFigures / numerical example\nAI reflection map", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#fff7dc", color="#93918c", tooltip="Check current foundations and QP exposition\nRead Chapters 2 and 4 against backlog items 1: terminology, Rudolf input/output, cyclic-word operation and dependence/vertex-replacement bridges. Return surviving/solved/withdrawn findings with exact source locations; no edits or theorem strengthening.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a bounded read-only Chapter 2/4 packet in its own worktree.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md\n\nCheck variation and HKO certificate navigation\nRead Chapters 6/7 and HKO appendix against backlog item 2; separate finite predicates and geometric implication. The certificate and slope-to-neighborhood proof are reported present. No certificate recomputation.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a bounded source-navigation review; coordinate Chapter 7 edits with the claim packet.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md\n\nCheck product-family finite and limiting proof bridges\nRead Chapters 9–11 against backlog item 3: ordered pairings, finite vertex/alternation calculations, equality classification, product-position squeeze and Hausdorff/capacity-continuity bridge. Preserve exact/numerical distinctions.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select an independent product-proof source packet; report exact surviving bridges before edits.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md\n\nDispose of reader concerns against the selected DS chapter\nMap retained human comments to current Chapter 8/appendix: applied, absent, context-accepted or older-draft-only. Preserve accepted correlation/area text, retrospective bounds and explicitly unresolved random_F8_s3_45. Human acceptance and overall DS scope remain separate.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a source-aware DS disposition packet; do not import old rejection as a current verdict.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md\n\nCheck visualization purposes and certified numerical example\nInspect Chapters 12–14 for panel purpose/inference limits and the requested concrete certified numerical example; return a scoped proposal using existing code/evidence without launching producers.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a read-only example/provenance design packet before implementing or running it.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md\n\nVerify AI annotation repairs against the selected source\nCheck selected Chapter 15 against the mapped v3 repairs; no confirmed annotation defect remains. Preserve factual disclosure separately from reflection and record source drift or unknown whole-chapter acceptance.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a bounded source-map check; do not rewrite unflagged AI prose.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md"];
  "__candidates_evidence" [label="EVIDENCE · READY IF SELECTED\nChapter 7 claim check\nCode correspondence\nArtifact traceability", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#fff7dc", color="#93918c", tooltip="Check rendered Chapter 7 claims and PDF/source identity\nIdentify source revision/PDF identity, then compare L10-N/L10-N+ rendered statement, equality family and upper-section-curvature caveat against 24 September disposition and non-HKO rational/analytic packet. If no matching PDF is available, report that prerequisite; do not treat the older frozen PDF as current.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: evidence\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select the bounded rendered-PDF claim audit; no expensive verifier rerun.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/consolidation/2026-09-24/claim-disposition.md, experiments/hko-local-maximum/non-hko/README.md, experiments/hko-local-maximum/non-hko/PROOF.md\n\nCheck retained algorithm and numerical contract boundaries\nTrace retained capacity/numerics/flow promises to crate APIs and focused evidence owners; distinguish theorem assumptions, bounded tests and optimized production correspondence. Return exact claim/contract gaps and recommended focused checks; no blanket implementation rewrite.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: evidence\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select read-only claim/API/evidence mapping in a separate worktree; test execution requires its chosen packet.\nSources: crates/README.md, docs/project-facts.md, ARCHITECTURE.md\n\nResolve displayed examples, counts and public artifact references\nMap named KKT/comparison/product counts, figures and annotated HKO listing to canonical packets and actual tracked/registered/public availability. Existing local files do not establish a public commit or remote download promise.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: evidence\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a bounded current-claim-to-artifact inventory; preserve producer-owned outputs.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md"];
  "__candidates_reproduction" [label="REPRODUCTION · READY IF SELECTED\nReproduction inventory", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#fff7dc", color="#93918c", tooltip="Compare the reproduction playbook with retained thesis promises\nInspect source-to-output-to-figure-to-PDF instructions, versions, LICCA timing/specs and comparison policies against the two-year target. Return complete/unknown/missing routes and cost estimates; no full producers or deletion experiment.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: reproduction\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a read-only playbook/output inventory; stage specific verification proposals afterward.\nSources: docs/reproducibility.md, docs/project-facts.md"];
  "__candidates_release" [label="RELEASE · READY IF SELECTED\nOfficial status check\nArchive preparation", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#fff7dc", color="#93918c", tooltip="Establish current submission status and official requirements\nPrepare a bounded check of current submission status, official rules and AI-disclosure requirements. Ask Jörn/current official sources when selected; never infer remaining hand-in or missed deadlines from historical notes.\nplan_gap: Unassigned and unselected; current administration/closure facts need inspection.\nproject: release\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select current status/rules inquiry; no external submission or message is authorized.\nSources: docs/project-facts.md, docs/coordination/handoff.md\n\nInventory closure-time rights, data and archive gaps\nCompare current payload/registry to accepted continuation/Zenodo checklist: rights notices, private/disposable material, useful artifacts, clean-cache materialization, exact reviewed commit/PDF, metadata and exterior publication. Return dispositions/questions without deleting, packing or publishing.\nplan_gap: Unassigned and unselected; current administration/closure facts need inspection.\nproject: release\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a bounded read-only closure inventory in its own worktree.\nSources: submit/archive-closure-checklist.md, docs/project-facts.md"];
